{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said to Moses, Pharaoh will not listen to you, etc.</b> He said that since the blessed El had told Moses that the reason for the hardening of heart that Pharaoh experienced — because YHWH hardened his spirit — was in order to multiply His signs, so that through them the Egyptians and Israel would recognize His greatness and goodness, as it says: וִידַעְתֶּם כִּי אֲנִי ה׳ (Exodus 10:2) — and to fulfill this intent Moses and Aaron together engaged in performing the signs — therefore now, when the blessed El decreed to punish the Egyptians and to deliver Israel from that punishment, even though some of them were in a sense deserving of it, and to bring down the gods of Egypt, so that the punishment might take effect — and all this through the Paschal sacrifice, as it says: וְעָבַרְתִּי וְהִכֵּיתִי, אֶעֱשֶׂה שְׁפָטִים, וּפָסַחְתִּי (Exodus 12:12–13) — He wanted this commandment to Israel to be carried out through Moses and Aaron together, just as they had labored together to bring the Egyptians to repentance and to instruct the children of Israel, so that both of them together would merit to bring to actuality the fruit of their endeavor."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:25:10.295030293Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}